<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung wins $2 bln IBM deal.</title>
<headline>Samsung wins $2 bln IBM deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Electronics Co has agreed to supply $2.0 billion worth of personal computer monitors to International Business Machines Corp over three years, Samsung sources said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Samsung Electronics, a unit of Samsung Group  SAGR.CN, will start shipping out the five million monitors next March, the sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have secured stable demand for PC monitors through the IBM deal,&quot; one of the sources said.</p>
<p>A Samsung spokesman declined to confirm or deny the deal.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom 9822) 727 5643</p>
